-- title:
--   Localisation at a horizontal prime is a valuation subring
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain with `IsDiscreteValuationRing`), let $F$ be a field equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure, and let $B$ be an $A_0$-subalgebra of $F$ subject to three hypotheses: $B$ is of finite type over $A_0$ (`B.FG`); every $x \in F$ integral over $B$ already lies in $B$; and every $x \in F$ admits $b, c \in B$ with $c \neq 0$ and $x c = b$, so that $F$ is the fraction field of $B$. Assume further that there is $t \in F$ such that every element of $F$ is algebraic over the $A_0$-subalgebra $A_0[t]$ generated by $t$. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime ideal of $B$ with $\mathfrak p \neq 0$ and such that the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ is not contained in $\mathfrak p$. The conclusion is the existence of a valuation subring $V$ of $F$ whose elements are exactly those $f \in F$ for which there are $b, c \in B$ with $c \notin \mathfrak p$ and $f c = b$; that is, the localisation $B_{\mathfrak p}$, realised inside $F$, is a valuation ring of $F$. No further property of $V$ (properness, principality) is asserted.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a nonzero prime of a normal, finite-type algebra of relative dimension at most one over a discrete valuation ring, lying in the generic fibre, has height one, so that the corresponding local ring is a valuation ring of the function field. It is pure commutative algebra, used to supply the normality/curve hypothesis in the construction of subalgebras of Drinfeld-type rings for modular curves of full level, which cites it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subalgebra_exists_valuationSubring_mem_iff_of_isPrime_of_not_map_maximalIdeal_le_of_isAlgebraic_adjoin.lean

